    "stdout": "[{\"type\": \"web_search_result\", \"title\": \"Igloo\", \"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Igloo\", \"content\": \"An igloo (\\n\\nKnown as the [igloo effect](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Igloo_effect), on the outside, temperatures may be as low as \\u221245 \\u00b0C (\\u221249 \\u00b0F), but on the inside, the temperature may range from \\u22127 to 16 \\u00b0C (19 to 61 \\u00b0F) when warmed by [body heat](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thermoregulation) alone. [[3]](./Igloo#cite_note-4)\\n\\n[[6]](./Igloo#cite_note-7)\\n\\n[[10]](./Igloo#cite_note-iglootce-11) [[11]](./Igloo#cite_note-polarp-12)\\n\\n[[10]](./Igloo#cite_note-iglootce-11) [[11]](./Igloo#cite_note-polarp-12) [[12]](./Igloo#cite_note-13)\\n\\n[[10]](./Igloo#cite_note-iglootce-11) [[11]](./Igloo#cite_note-polarp-12)\\n\\n[[10]](./Igloo#cite_note-iglootce-11) [[11]](./Igloo#cite_note-polarp-12)\\n\\n[[13]](./Igloo#cite_note-handy-14)\\n\\n[[13]](./Igloo#cite_note-handy-14)\\n\\n[[15]](./Igloo#cite_note-A&N-16)\\nSnow's insulating properties enable the inside of the igloo to remain relatively warm.\\n\\n[[15]](./Igloo#cite_note-A&N-16) Sometimes, a short tunnel is constructed at the entrance, to reduce wind and heat loss when the door is opened.\\n\\n[[16]](./Igloo#cite_note-vol1-17) by making a large flame with a [qulliq](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qulliq) (kudlik, stone lamp), briefly making the interior very hot, which causes the walls to melt slightly and settle. [[15]](./Igloo#cite_note-A&N-16) Body heat is also adequate, although slower.\\n\\n\n",
